# Accounts the IONIS units run as. systemd-sysusers creates them at install, so the timers have
# an account to run as on ANY host — including a stranger's, installing from Copr. Before 4.0.8
# the units named `ki7mt`, a human account that exists only on one lab's control node, so they
# could not start anywhere else.
#
# IDS ARE ALLOCATED AUTOMATICALLY ("-"), as sysusers.d(5) counsels: "strongly recommended unless
# it is strictly necessary to use a specific UID or GID". It is not necessary here, and nothing
# downstream should infer that pinning is what a careful deployment does.
#
# The rule worth carrying: PIN ONLY WHEN SOMETHING OUTSIDE YOUR CONTROL ALREADY FIXED THE NUMBER
# — a container image, a vendor appliance, an upstream that hardcodes it. Nothing here is in that
# class. (An earlier revision of this comment claimed the lab pins these because its data is
# backed up and replicated. That justification did not survive checking — zfs send streams
# restore onto a host whose accounts already exist, nothing NFS-exports those directories — and
# the lab does not pin them either. Recorded rather than deleted, because the claim shipped.)
#
# ionis-report is deliberately NOT here: it belongs to morning-health-check, which lives in
# fleet-ops, not in this package. The two account lists differ on purpose.
g ionis-data   -
u ionis-ingest -:ionis-data "IONIS ingest pipelines" /var/lib/ionis-ingest /sbin/nologin
